WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.492
Checkpoint question. What makes the plain Python workflow agentic?

00:00:05.492 --> 00:00:08.107
It is not the vector database.

00:00:08.107 --> 00:00:11.757
A vector database can exist in classic rag.

00:00:11.757 --> 00:00:15.892
It is not using the largest possible language model.

00:00:15.892 --> 00:00:21.065
The agentic behavior comes from state plus conditional next-step decisions.

00:00:21.515 --> 00:00:29.872
The workflow remembers what has happened, inspects the result, and chooses whether to generate, rewrite, retrieve again,

00:00:29.872 --> 00:00:35.754
or stop. So the correct answer is: state plus conditional decisions.
